The smoke procedure is this package's only third-party-client evidence — the Vitest suite talks to the server in-process — and its documented contract (the readiness record's shape and default path, the loopback port and MCP route, the five tools' input schemas and annotation hints) must match the implementation, which nothing automated compares it against; the implementation is authoritative, so a transport, HTTP-composition, or tool-surface change is re-verified by re-running the procedure and updating its expected outputs.
